{"id": 1950, "name": "Lamar City Park", "read": "2026-10-15", "pages": [{"url": "https://cityoflamar.org/m/faq?cat=19#question-102", "lines": ["elter 3 (across from the playground by the basketball courts) and Shelter 6 (small memorial shelter across from the outfield of the high school baseball field) are all available to reserve for smaller events. There is a $25 deposit required to reserve, that is refundable, as long as all trash from your event is in the trash cans and no park property is damaged. The Enclosed Shelter also requires a $25 rental fee. She", "reserve for smaller events. There is a $25 deposit required to reserve, that is refundable, as long as all trash from your event is in the trash cans and no park property is damaged. The Enclosed Shelter also requires a $25 rental fee. Shelters 4, 5 and 7 at the City Park and the Shelter at Wheeler Park are available on a first-come, first-served basis. We do ask if you will have a group of more than 50 using one of ", ". There is a frost free hydrant available for filling by the green bathroom facility and a central dumping station on the southwest edge of the RV area. The first night you stay with us is free, each additional night is $20 up to a seven day maximum stay. There is currently no overnight camping allowed at the Lamar City Lake and no tent camping is allowed at any city facility. | Parks & Recreation | How do I rent a b", "nd boating permits are good from January through December each year. They can be purchased in person at City Hall or the Parks and Recreation Office or online through our online catalog in the activities tab. Fishing is $30 per year, boating is $45 per year. Non-motorized boats (canoes, kayaks, paddle boats) do need a permit, however it is just $10 per year. | Daily fishing and boating permits can be purchased by usi", "and Recreation Office or online through our online catalog in the activities tab. Fishing is $30 per year, boating is $45 per year. Non-motorized boats (canoes, kayaks, paddle boats) do need a permit, however it is just $10 per year. | Daily fishing and boating permits can be purchased by using the drop box at the Lake Office on the south side of the lake or by using our online catalog in the activities tab. | Parks ", "6 hours) or whole day (any time period over 6 hours). There is a deposit required to reserve your space and reservations can be made at any time in advance of your event. Alcohol is permitted in the meeting rooms with a $200 alcohol fee, $100 of which is refundable. | To see the full pricing or to reserve Thiebaud for your next event, please visit our online catalog ! | Parks & Recreation | How do I get a message on ", "stage, two backstage dressing rooms, stage lighting and sound, a projector and screen, as well as an array of microphone and monitors to help you have the best performance or meeting. | Thiebaud is available to rent for $50 per hour for non-ticketed events or $400 or 10 percent of ticket sales for ticketed events. Lamar Schools are provided use of the Auditorium for a discounted rate as well. | Thiebaud has been used"]}, {"url": "https://cityoflamar.org/101/Services", "lines": [], "via": "Services"}, {"url": "https://cityoflamar.org/177/TATS", "lines": [" 3-mile radius of the City of Lamar. Medical trips for the elderly and disabled who have no other means of transportation are provided county-wide. Twenty-four hour notice is required for these medical trips. | Pricing: $4 per stop / $2 per stop for Seniors or Disabled Individuals | Limit 4 one-way trips per day. | Notifying the Public of Rights Under Title VI Service: | T.A.T.S. operates its programs and services wi"], "via": "Truman Area Transportation Service"}]}
{"id": 1951, "name": "Osceola RV Park and Campground", "read": "2026-10-15", "pages": [{"url": "https://cityofosceolamo.com/rv-park---campground.html", "lines": []}, {"url": "https://cityofosceolamo.com/rv-park-prices.html", "lines": [" | Economic Development | City Ordinances | Attractions & Photos | CITY CALENDAR | Weather Information | LANDLORD LISTING | Annual Water Quality | City of Osceola, MO | OTHER SERVICES AVAILABLE: | Dump Station/USE ONLY: $5.00 | Showers (non-park residents): $5.00 | OZZIE Building Rental: $80.00* | | (* Ozzie rental fee includes a $40.00 refundable deposit ) | | | | | RV or Boat STORAGE (storage area fees only): | $1.", "Dump Station/USE ONLY: $5.00 | Showers (non-park residents): $5.00 | OZZIE Building Rental: $80.00* | | (* Ozzie rental fee includes a $40.00 refundable deposit ) | | | | | RV or Boat STORAGE (storage area fees only): | $1.50/day | | | Rates are calculated per night for 2 adults and children age 15 or under that are in the same camper/tent. Separate vehicles/campers/tents on the same site are charged at the same rate", "d children age 15 or under that are in the same camper/tent. Separate vehicles/campers/tents on the same site are charged at the same rate as another site. | | | | RV Park & Campground Rates | WATER, SEWER, & ELECTRIC - $22.00 | | | | WATER & ELECTRIC ONLY - $20.00 | | | | TENT SPACE (Primitive) - $15.00 | | | | City of Osceola © 2013 All Rights Reserved | View on Mobile"], "via": "PRICES"}, {"url": "https://cityofosceolamo.com/rv-park-rules.html", "lines": [" outdoor activities. | OZZIE GUILFORD BUILDING: | | Named in memory of one of Osceola's former mayors, and an avid supporter of the park. Mr. Guildford assisted in building the hall. The hall can be rented for any event $80.00/day, which includes a $40.00 deposit (refundable if the building is left clean and tidy). RV Camping Clubs have free use of the clubhouse for social interaction. | YOUR CAMPSITE: | | Everyone i", "r immediately. | | Fires are allowed in the fire rings. Please do NOT throw household trash, bottles or cans in the fire. Remove all trash and place in receptacles, NOT IN THE FIRE RING. | | Ice is available for sale at $1.75/bag. | | Campers will take full responsibility for the actions of their guests in the park. All campers and guests should practice good camping manners. | | Disorderly conduct, drunkenness, vulg"], "via": "RULES"}, {"url": "https://cityofosceolamo.com/rv-park-map.html", "lines": [], "via": "​RV Park Map"}]}
